<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jai Narayan Vyas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1899–1963</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jai Narayan Vyas was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-independence">Indian independence</a> activist and politician from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jodhpur">Jodhpur</a> who led the Marwar Lok Parishad, the movement for responsible government in the princely state of Marwar. After the formation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a> he became its chief minister in 1951–1952 and again from 1952 to 1954, as a leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-national-congress">Indian National Congress</a>.</p></div>
